{"id": "EUVD-2026-82257", "enisaUuid": "cceb8c22-0729-3161-bfa5-0ae3f1821a87", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211_hwsim: avoid NULL skb in stop queue drain\n\nmac80211_hwsim_stop() drops any frames left in data->pending. The loop\ncurrently checks skb_queue_empty() and then dequeues separately.\n\nThat split is racy with TX status handling, which can remove a pending\nframe under the queue lock. If the last entry is removed after the empty\ncheck, skb_dequeue() returns NULL and the stop path passes that NULL skb\nto ieee80211_free_txskb().\n\nUse skb_dequeue() as the loop condition instead. The dequeue result is the\nobject that stop owns and frees, and a concurrent status completion that\nempties the queue simply makes the loop terminate.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:06:21", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d131027054a8dd922dda01fe8d381abe5af4970b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c40ba47f2ba1951cb32ea048667ed014d36a5749", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2817431a61557f46dc63077b7cc126bc906c242e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7fccad2c8e6ef6bbafe509c95869d161d0f466b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c2a4ab6efa26415dd131b8c222e7893fda03435", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/158438cd6ad69d6dd7d871582c38baf22169fede"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93149", "GHSA-9v89-8pp7-7fmp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1eefa896-29c3-300e-bee4-d4548707ab5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd18de517923903a177508fc8813f44e717b1c00 <1c2a4ab6efa26415dd131b8c222e7893fda03435"}, {"id": "2510b278-db1c-3a42-95fd-d7aa428c8618", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9028333001f793b2724e8be42fce3336de2cf1c"}, {"id": "2da48163-4f5f-3390-8cf9-ee45d19ff8da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "78bf3c6131488b00386acd9aff1ea4e6c44fa38e"}, {"id": "42ffd5f0-4f05-346e-8633-cb16ae5710c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7019c9f385b264a2d6f685028268422d55087e37"}, {"id": "43df977f-10cc-3329-9c13-320e86f8159f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "5492040a-49db-3070-b885-6f081c966fe7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4.129 <5.5"}, {"id": "5788b901-01e6-3c96-ad1a-9c7ab8d67a10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "8085361c-440f-3361-adc5-0bb8ede06fc4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "80b8748e-8913-3197-b733-dd836060de49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd18de517923903a177508fc8813f44e717b1c00 <158438cd6ad69d6dd7d871582c38baf22169fede"}, {"id": "97b48dcc-017b-35ad-a60f-4da40e8074b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13"}, {"id": "a8c5a88f-a166-3347-a002-dbad52281cab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "b13faa9c-2e6b-39bb-b73f-46284aa767b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd18de517923903a177508fc8813f44e717b1c00 <c40ba47f2ba1951cb32ea048667ed014d36a5749"}, {"id": "bbe0a658-a080-3e80-bc1d-152c0997deb1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d13b578a-5e04-37ff-91da-7e082a0cdb46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd18de517923903a177508fc8813f44e717b1c00 <2817431a61557f46dc63077b7cc126bc906c242e"}, {"id": "e50e0d95-dfeb-3807-9e80-c859d23b7626", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e57e741a-8